      "problem": "Simplify the statement $¬(P∧Q)⇒(P∧R).$",
      "worked_solution": "First, note that\n\n$$\n¬(P∧Q)⇒(P∧R)≡¬(¬(P∧Q))∨(P∧R).\n$$\n\nCanceling out double negations, we reach\n\n$$\n¬(¬(P∧Q))∨(P∧R)≡(P∧Q)∨(P∧R).\n$$\n\nFinally, by the distributive laws, we have\n\n$$\n(P∧Q)∨(P∧R)≡P∧(Q∨R).\n$$\n\nSo the given statement is equivalent to $P∧(Q∨R).$",
